// Title: Suspicious Key Manager Access
// Sigma ID: a4694263-59a8-4608-a3a0-6f8d3a51664c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-21 | Modified: 2023-02-09
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555.004
// Description: Detects the invocation of the Stored User Names and Passwords dialogue (Key Manager)
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/NinjaParanoid/status/1516442028963659777
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_keymgr.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "keymgr" and ProcessCommandLine contains "KRShowKeyMgr")
